到最后，你这辈子都不想再吃冰淇淋蛋糕了。

463
00:19:19.410 --> 00:19:24.850
I mean, for years, lady, for years, I could not eat like ice cream,
我是说，好几年啊，女士，好几年，在那一集之后，我都没法吃冰淇淋，

464
00:19:25.230 --> 00:19:27.710
anything like ice cream related after that episode.
任何跟冰淇淋有关的东西都吃不了。

465
00:19:28.010 --> 00:19:29.350
It really turned on me.
它真的让我反胃了。

466
00:19:29.450 --> 00:19:30.330
They had to get me a bucket.
他们不得不给我拿个桶来。

467
00:19:30.870 --> 00:19:31.990
Oh, lady, same.
哦，女士，我也是。

468
00:19:32.290 --> 00:19:32.630
Yeah.
是啊。

469
00:19:32.990 --> 00:19:33.370
Same.
我也是。

470
00:19:33.670 --> 00:19:34.870
That was really tough.
那真的太难熬了。

471
00:19:35.250 --> 00:19:40.670
And then do you remember I was trying to figure out the episode where the party planning committee,
你还记得吗，我一直在想那一集，就是派对策划委员会的那集，

472
00:19:40.670 --> 00:19:45.970
I think it was a Christmas episode, where they had all the chocolates and chocolate boxes.
我想应该是圣诞特辑，他们有很多巧克力和巧克力盒。

473
00:19:46.330 --> 00:19:47.010
Oh, yeah.
哦，记得。

474
00:19:47.410 --> 00:19:51.450
And Ed Helms and Mindy, who were notorious for eating prop food,
艾德·赫尔姆斯和敏迪，他们俩以爱吃道具食物出名，

475
00:19:51.930 --> 00:19:54.630
started digging into the chocolates and one had maggots in it.
开始大吃特吃那些巧克力，结果其中一个里面有蛆。

476
00:19:55.090 --> 00:19:57.430
Oh, yes, I remember this.
哦，对，我记得这件事。

477
00:19:57.550 --> 00:19:57.750
Yes.
没错。

478
00:19:57.750 --> 00:20:00.450
Because they did not intend for us to eat them.
因为他们根本没打算让我们吃那些东西。

479
00:20:00.650 --> 00:20:01.230
Yes.
是的。

480
00:20:01.370 --> 00:20:03.030
It was supposed to be scent decoration.
那本来只是装饰用的。

481
00:20:03.330 --> 00:20:06.310
And Mindy and Ed started to go.
结果敏迪和艾德就开始吃了。

482
00:20:08.360 --> 00:20:09.320
Oh, my God.
天哪。

483
00:20:09.320 --> 00:20:10.940
We freaked out.
我们都吓坏了。

484
00:20:10.940 --> 00:20:13.600
We're like, ah, oh, it was so disgusting.
我们当时反应是，啊，天哪，太恶心了。

485
00:20:13.980 --> 00:20:17.680
Well, now that's bringing up a memory for me where I can't remember what it was.
好吧，这让我想起了一件事，但我记不清具体是什么了。

486
00:20:17.920 --> 00:20:23.220
I feel like, because it was me and BJ, BJ also loved to eat prop food.
我觉得，因为当时是我和BJ，BJ也喜欢吃道具食物。

487
00:20:23.440 --> 00:20:26.200
And there was like a big buffet of food.
当时有一大桌自助餐。

488
00:20:26.720 --> 00:20:28.100
Gosh, it might have been.
天哪，可能是那次吧。

489
00:20:28.440 --> 00:20:29.240
Was it Diwali?
是排灯节那集吗？

490
00:20:29.660 --> 00:20:30.700
No, no, no, no.
不，不，不，不是。

491
00:20:30.780 --> 00:20:32.000
It was in the conference room.
是在会议室里。

492
00:20:32.280 --> 00:20:36.240
Oh, I wish I could remember, but it was a conference room scene and there's tons of food.
哦，我真希望我能想起来，但那是一场会议室的戏，有很多食物。

493
00:20:36.360 --> 00:20:40.180
But like the storyline is that we're actually not wanting to eat it.
剧情设定是我们其实不想吃那些东西。

494
00:20:40.180 --> 00:20:42.320
I can't remember why, what this is.
我不记得为什么了，想不起来是什么戏。

495
00:20:42.660 --> 00:20:44.880
Someone out there is probably like shouting it out right now.
屏幕前的观众现在可能正在大声喊出答案呢。

496
00:20:45.640 --> 00:20:50.220
But because that food was going to stay out for a long period of time, they had kind of
但因为那些食物要摆放很长时间，他们往上面喷了些东西，

497
00:20:50.220 --> 00:20:56.460
sprayed something on it to keep it safe, like under the lights, so it wouldn't get super
为了在灯光下保持安全，不会变得特别

498
00:20:56.460 --> 00:20:57.420
nasty and smell.
恶心或者发臭。

499
00:20:58.200 --> 00:21:00.460
But you were not supposed to eat it.
但你是不应该吃它们的。

500
00:21:01.020 --> 00:21:06.520
And BJ and I, like between takes, we were like picking at the buffet.
而我和BJ在拍摄间隙，还在那儿偷吃自助餐。

501
00:21:07.320 --> 00:21:11.320
And they had to run over and be like, no, no, no, no, do not eat that.
他们不得不跑过去说，不，不，不，不，别吃那个。

502
00:21:11.480 --> 00:21:14.380
That is, it's not even prop food.
那甚至都不是道具食物。

503
00:21:14.400 --> 00:21:16.300
It's like decorative food.
那就像是装饰用的食物。

504
00:21:16.440 --> 00:21:16.640
Yeah.
是啊。

505
00:21:16.780 --> 00:21:18.500
They're like, don't eat the decorative food.
他们就像是说，别吃那些装饰用的食物。

506
00:21:18.620 --> 00:21:20.320
And they had shellacked it with something.
而且他们还在上面刷了层虫胶漆之类的东西。

507
00:21:20.560 --> 00:21:22.220
Yes, which is like what those chocolates were.
没错，就像那些巧克力一样。

508
00:21:22.340 --> 00:21:23.340
Those were like decoration.
那些也是装饰品。

509
00:21:23.820 --> 00:21:24.120
Yeah.
是啊。

510
00:21:24.400 --> 00:21:24.580
Yeah.
没错。

511
00:21:24.900 --> 00:21:25.360
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

512
00:21:25.520 --> 00:21:25.960
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

513
00:21:25.960 --> 00:21:31.900
Well, I feel like for the most part, I was really spared from having to eat anything
我觉得大部分时候，我真的很幸运，没被迫吃什么

514
00:21:31.900 --> 00:21:32.200
gross.
恶心的东西。

515
00:21:32.380 --> 00:21:36.080
Like I think about you guys and those hot dogs on beach games.
比如我想到你们在海滩游戏里吃的那些热狗。

516
00:21:36.340 --> 00:21:39.760
My character was a vegetarian when she needed to be.
我的角色在需要的时候是个素食主义者。

517
00:21:40.800 --> 00:21:42.300
I mean, we've discussed that.
我是说，我们讨论过这个。

518
00:21:42.420 --> 00:21:43.840
Sometimes she is, sometimes she isn't.
有时候她是，有时候她不是。

519
00:21:43.940 --> 00:21:46.020
But so I did not eat the hot dogs.
所以我没吃那些热狗。

520
00:21:46.200 --> 00:21:48.720
I didn't either because I was taking my diligent notes.
我也没有，因为我当时在认真做笔记。

521
00:21:49.000 --> 00:21:49.220
Yeah.
是啊。

522
00:21:49.500 --> 00:21:52.820
But a bunch of people did and they got real grossed out.
但很多人吃了，他们觉得恶心坏了。

523
00:21:52.820 --> 00:21:56.740
I remember when it turned on them, a hot dog turning on you.
我记得当热狗开始让人反胃的时候，那种感觉。

524
00:21:56.940 --> 00:21:57.380
Outside.
在户外。

525
00:21:57.380 --> 00:21:59.200
And it was hot out there.
而且外面天气很热。

526
00:21:59.740 --> 00:22:01.680
Eating all those hot dogs in the hot sun.
在烈日下吃那么多热狗。

527
00:22:02.000 --> 00:22:02.280
Ah.
啊。

528
00:22:02.520 --> 00:22:06.160
Well, one of the people who had to do the most eating on our show was Rainn Wilson.
嗯，我们剧里吃东西最多的人之一是雷恩·威尔森。

529
00:22:06.400 --> 00:22:07.920
Wait, can I just stop you right there?
等等，我能打断一下吗？

530
00:22:08.040 --> 00:22:08.660
What is it?
怎么了？

531
00:22:08.720 --> 00:22:12.200
Had to do a lot of eating or chose to do a lot of eating.
是不得不吃很多，还是选择吃很多？

532
00:22:12.360 --> 00:22:12.500
Both.
两者都有。

533
00:22:12.660 --> 00:22:13.720
I think both.
我觉得两者都有。

534
00:22:13.920 --> 00:22:14.940
Definitely both.
绝对是两者都有。

535
00:22:15.140 --> 00:22:19.400
Because when he commits, he goes all out and he didn't have to eat as much as he did.
因为他一旦投入，就会全力以赴，其实他根本不需要吃那么多。

536
00:22:19.400 --> 00:22:26.740
Well, before I left town, I had lunch with Rainn and after our lunch, we sat in my car
嗯，在我离开城里之前，我和雷恩吃了午饭，午饭后，我们坐在我的车里，

537
00:22:26.740 --> 00:22:30.740
and he shared his on and off set food memories with me.
他和我分享了他片场内外的食物记忆。

538
00:22:30.900 --> 00:22:31.660
It was really sweet.
真的很温馨。

539
00:22:31.760 --> 00:22:32.860
I want you guys to hear it.
我想让你们听听。

540
00:22:33.000 --> 00:22:33.240
Okay.
好的。

541
00:22:34.020 --> 00:22:37.680
Hey, office ladies, people, listeners.
嘿，办公室女士们，各位听众。

542
00:22:38.040 --> 00:22:38.940
This is Rainn.
我是雷恩。

543
00:22:39.540 --> 00:22:40.340
Hi, Rainn.
嗨，雷恩。

544
00:22:40.620 --> 00:22:41.560
It's Jenna.
我是珍娜。

545
00:22:41.840 --> 00:22:42.780
Jenna Fisher.
珍娜·费舍尔。

546
00:22:43.040 --> 00:22:43.760
I'm with you.
我和你在一起。

547
00:22:43.940 --> 00:22:45.340
We just had lunch.
我们刚吃完午饭。

548
00:22:45.340 --> 00:22:54.680
And Jenna brought her sound recording equipment, this very fancy TASCOM recorder with lots of
珍娜带了她的录音设备，这个非常高级的塔斯肯录音机，连着很多

549
00:22:54.680 --> 00:22:57.620
fancy cables and a big mic attached to it.
高级的线缆和一个大麦克风。

550
00:22:57.720 --> 00:22:59.680
And then she forgot to put a...
然后她忘了装一个……

551
00:22:59.680 --> 00:23:01.820
Like, I guess the SIM card thing in it?
比如，我想是里面那个SIM卡的问题？

552
00:23:01.860 --> 00:23:02.700
The card in it.
里面的那张卡。

553
00:23:02.880 --> 00:23:04.540
So we're recording it on my phone.
所以我们现在正用我的手机录音。

554
00:23:04.920 --> 00:23:06.420
And this is...
而这……

555
00:23:06.420 --> 00:23:07.460
Yes.
是的。

556
00:23:07.740 --> 00:23:09.080
Well, we just ate food.
嗯，我们刚吃完饭。

557
00:23:09.240 --> 00:23:09.600
Pathetic.
真可怜。

558
00:23:09.600 --> 00:23:14.780
You said we're doing an episode about office food and you have some good stories because
你说我们要录一期关于办公室食物的节目，而且你有一些很棒的故事，因为

559
00:23:14.780 --> 00:23:21.280
you had the very unique position of having both insane food storylines written for you
你处于一个非常独特的境地，既要演那些为你写的疯狂的食物剧情，

560
00:23:21.280 --> 00:23:22.900
where you had to eat crazy things.
还得被迫吃下那些奇怪的东西。

561
00:23:22.900 --> 00:23:29.020
But then also you made some choices that you maybe...
但同时你也做出了一些选择，可能……

562
00:23:29.020 --> 00:23:29.740
I did.
我确实做了。

563
00:23:29.960 --> 00:23:30.220
I did.
我确实做了。

564
00:23:30.440 --> 00:23:30.820
Had to deal with.
不得不去应对。

565
00:23:31.160 --> 00:23:34.780
But first of all, I want to say that you had breakfast for lunch today.
但首先，我想说你今天午餐吃了早餐。

566
00:23:35.100 --> 00:23:35.680
I did.
我确实吃了。

567
00:23:35.820 --> 00:23:36.140
Yeah.
没错。

568
00:23:36.140 --> 00:23:41.740
So we had lunch and then Jenna had the avocado toast with poached eggs and bacon.
我们吃了午饭，然后珍娜点了牛油果吐司，配水波蛋和培根。

569
00:23:41.980 --> 00:23:46.820
I wanted both eggs and bacon on my avocado toast at 1.30 p.m.
下午一点半，我就想在牛油果吐司上加蛋和培根。

570
00:23:46.820 --> 00:23:47.640
She went for it.
她真的这么做了。

571
00:23:47.780 --> 00:23:50.680
And it was glorious to see.
看着真是太棒了。

572
00:23:50.720 --> 00:23:53.900
I love a woman with that appetite.
我喜欢胃口好的女性。

573
00:23:54.140 --> 00:23:54.720
Yes.
没错。

574
00:23:54.720 --> 00:23:57.020
I've never denied my appetite.
我从不否认我的胃口。

575
00:23:57.020 --> 00:23:58.260
I can't do it.
我可做不到。

576
00:23:58.680 --> 00:24:00.500
I like it.
我喜欢这样。

577
00:24:00.680 --> 00:24:01.260
Too much.
太多了。

578
00:24:01.440 --> 00:24:03.380
And Dwight has his appetites.
德怀特也有他的胃口。

579
00:24:03.400 --> 00:24:04.440
Yes, he certainly does.
是的，他确实有。

580
00:24:04.440 --> 00:24:07.600
Yeah, no, your question was right on because here's the thing.
没错，不，你问得太对了，因为情况是这样的。

581
00:24:07.700 --> 00:24:12.080
One of the things that really bugs me about actors is when you're watching a movie and
作为演员，有一件事真的很让我困扰，就是当你在看电影时，

582
00:24:12.080 --> 00:24:15.980
you can see that the actors aren't really eating in a meal scene, they're like pushing
你能看出演员在用餐场景里并没有真的在吃，他们只是在盘子里

583
00:24:15.980 --> 00:24:17.080
the food around on their plates.
拨弄食物。

584
00:24:17.200 --> 00:24:18.740
They're pushing the peas around or whatever.
他们拨弄着豌豆之类的东西。

585
00:24:19.320 --> 00:24:22.520
Because, you know, when you're shooting a scene, you have to shoot like 12 different
因为你知道，拍摄一场戏时，你得拍大概12个不同的

586
00:24:22.520 --> 00:24:24.020
takes and lots of different versions.
镜头，还有很多不同的版本。

587
00:24:24.020 --> 00:24:25.740
And, you know, and I get it.
而且，你知道，我理解。

588
00:24:25.840 --> 00:24:33.300
People don't want to like be eating enormous mouthfuls of food because if you do 12 takes,
人们不想大口大口地吃东西，因为如果你拍12条，

589
00:24:33.480 --> 00:24:37.080
then that's, you know, 12 times however many mouthfuls of food.
那就是，你知道，12乘以好几大口的食物量。

590
00:24:37.500 --> 00:24:39.540
But that's one thing that's always bugged me.
但这一直是我很介意的一点。

591
00:24:39.620 --> 00:24:44.440
So I've always kind of as an actor prided myself on like committing to eating.
所以作为演员，我一直以全身心投入进食而自豪。

592
00:24:44.720 --> 00:24:46.260
Well, I appreciate it.
嗯，我很欣赏这一点。

593
00:24:46.260 --> 00:24:52.000
I mean, how fun is it to watch all of those great actors and like Goodfellas and The Godfather
我是说，看那些伟大的演员，比如在《好家伙》和《教父》里，

594
00:24:52.000 --> 00:24:57.500
just like devour, devour their big Italian meals and their steak.
看着他们狼吞虎咽地吃下丰盛的意大利餐和牛排，多有意思啊。

595
00:24:57.820 --> 00:25:00.360
Like it's so satisfying to watch.
看起来真是太满足了。

596
00:25:00.540 --> 00:25:01.280
Yeah, yeah.
是啊，是啊。

597
00:25:01.280 --> 00:25:06.500
And they were always trying to think of ways to have Dwight eating because I think they
他们总是想方设法让德怀特吃东西，因为我想他们

598
00:25:06.500 --> 00:25:10.720
saw that I fully committed kind of ravenously to the enterprise.
看出了我非常投入，几乎是如饥似渴地对待这份工作。

599
00:25:10.880 --> 00:25:17.680
I think my favorite food memory was the breakfast that I had with Jan when I was planning to,
我想我最喜欢的食物记忆是和简一起吃的早餐，当时我正计划着，

600
00:25:17.900 --> 00:25:21.380
the Crentist episode when I was planning to overthrow Michael.
就是那个“牙医”那一集，当时我正计划推翻迈克尔。

601
00:25:21.720 --> 00:25:30.000
And I had pancakes and eggs and toast and waffles and I cover the whole thing with syrup.
我当时吃了煎饼、鸡蛋、吐司和华夫饼，而且我在上面淋满了糖浆。

602
00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:32.100
Now, that was your choice.
那是你自己的选择。

603
00:25:32.320 --> 00:25:36.800
That was not in the script that you covered it all with syrup for a long time, right?
剧本里可没写你要在那儿淋那么久的糖浆，对吧？

604
00:25:37.060 --> 00:25:37.740
Or was it?
还是说写了？

605
00:25:37.820 --> 00:25:38.520
We don't remember.
我们不记得了。

606
00:25:38.840 --> 00:25:41.800
I think it was in the script.
我觉得剧本里写了。

607
00:25:41.940 --> 00:25:44.580
And I remember Paul Lieberstein talking to me about it,
我记得保罗·利伯斯坦跟我谈过这件事，

608
00:25:44.780 --> 00:25:51.060
about the idea of like locking eyes with her and then just pouring syrup for far too long.
关于那种和她对视然后不停地倒糖浆的构思。

609
00:25:51.220 --> 00:25:57.160
But I don't think he insisted that I eat as much as I actually ate in the course of the scene.
但我觉得他并没有坚持要求我在那场戏里吃掉那么多东西。

610
00:25:57.160 --> 00:26:01.500
And I did dig in to those pancakes.
但我确实大口大口地吃那些煎饼了。

611
00:26:01.640 --> 00:26:04.320
I'll never forget that flavor.
我永远忘不了那个味道。

612
00:26:04.600 --> 00:26:06.460
And I'm so glad I did.
我很高兴我那么做了。

613
00:26:06.460 --> 00:26:08.720
It was so much fun.
那真的很有趣。

614
00:26:09.000 --> 00:26:16.980
And I think Melora, I think it kind of blew her mind exactly how many pounds of pancakes I ate during that scene.
我觉得梅罗拉当时肯定被我那场戏里吃掉的几磅煎饼给惊到了。

615
00:26:16.980 --> 00:26:24.080
But what about the scene where Dwight is eating all of his like about to spoil food?
那德怀特吃掉那些快要变质的食物的戏呢？

616
00:26:24.360 --> 00:26:25.220
All of his...
他所有的……

617
00:26:25.220 --> 00:26:25.270
Right.
没错。

618
00:26:25.440 --> 00:26:28.180
From like the fallout shelter or his survival shelter.
就是从那个防空洞或者生存避难所里拿出来的。

