00:48:02.130 --> 00:48:04.050
This makes me sad.
这让我很难过。

1103
00:48:04.670 --> 00:48:04.720
I know.
我知道。

1104
00:48:04.850 --> 00:48:08.470
This is sort of like foreshadowing for dinner party.
这有点像是晚宴的前奏。

1105
00:48:08.670 --> 00:48:10.090
So much foreshadowing.
铺垫得太多了。

1106
00:48:10.370 --> 00:48:15.150
Well, that was the pitch for lunch slash the nooner.
好吧，那本来是午餐兼午间小憩的提议。

1107
00:48:15.150 --> 00:48:19.110
Can you guess what the tag was going to be for this episode?
你能猜到这一集的片尾彩蛋原本是什么吗？

1108
00:48:19.390 --> 00:48:21.650
You guessed Stanley sleeping in his car.
你猜的是斯坦利在车里睡觉。

1109
00:48:22.630 --> 00:48:26.290
There's going to be another moment in a car.
之后还有一个关于车的桥段。

1110
00:48:28.250 --> 00:48:29.370
Oh, Lord.
噢，天哪。

1111
00:48:29.590 --> 00:48:33.090
Is it like Andy getting a handjob from Meredith?
是安迪被梅雷迪斯那啥了吗？

1112
00:48:33.470 --> 00:48:34.050
Yes!
没错！

1113
00:48:36.010 --> 00:48:39.050
Andy and Meredith have sex in her car.
安迪和梅雷迪斯在她的车里发生了关系。

1114
00:48:39.550 --> 00:48:41.470
That was the tag.
那原本是片尾彩蛋。

1115
00:48:41.810 --> 00:48:43.230
I had no idea.
我完全不知道。

1116
00:48:43.230 --> 00:48:45.930
I just completely threw that out there.
我刚才只是随口一说。

1117
00:48:46.070 --> 00:48:46.650
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1118
00:48:47.430 --> 00:48:47.910
Wow.
哇。

1119
00:48:48.270 --> 00:48:51.650
Well, a lunch episode would have packed some surprises.
好吧，午餐那一集本来会有不少惊喜。

1120
00:48:52.210 --> 00:48:52.550
Yes.
是的。

1121
00:48:52.910 --> 00:48:53.630
Pretty fun.
挺有趣的。

1122
00:48:54.430 --> 00:48:56.230
Well, speaking of lunch.
说到午餐。

1123
00:48:57.150 --> 00:48:58.630
I want to hear this segue.
我想听听这个转场。

1124
00:48:59.070 --> 00:49:02.970
You know, before the break, we talked a lot about the food and the world of the office,
你知道，休息前我们聊了很多关于食物和《办公室》世界的事，

1125
00:49:03.250 --> 00:49:04.410
the stuff we had to eat and scenes.
我们在拍摄场景中吃的东西。

1126
00:49:04.550 --> 00:49:09.690
But there was a whole other world behind the scenes, our amazing catering and craft service.
但幕后还有另一个世界，那就是我们出色的餐饮和茶点服务团队。

1127
00:49:10.050 --> 00:49:10.370
Yes.
没错。

1128
00:49:10.550 --> 00:49:11.570
They were wonderful.
他们太棒了。

1129
00:49:12.050 --> 00:49:16.550
There's part of our book, The Office BFFs, where we share about craft service,
我们的书《办公室闺蜜》里有一部分专门讲了茶点服务，

1130
00:49:16.650 --> 00:49:20.570
and catering, and like what meals look like on the set.
还有餐饮，以及片场用餐是什么样的。

1131
00:49:20.710 --> 00:49:21.990
And I'm so glad it's there.
我很高兴书里写了这些。

1132
00:49:22.430 --> 00:49:28.130
Craft services and Peter and Vartan and Sergio and catering and his team were such a big part
茶点服务团队的彼得、瓦尔坦、塞尔吉奥，还有餐饮团队，他们是我们《办公室》大家庭的重要组成部分。

1133
00:49:28.130 --> 00:49:30.450
of our community on the office.
我们已经在书《办公室闺蜜》里写过了。

1134
00:49:30.630 --> 00:49:32.950
We wrote about it in our book, The Office BFFs.
我们已经在书《办公室闺蜜》里写过了。

1135
00:49:32.950 --> 00:49:39.150
And we both have really special memories, as does the whole cast and crew, of mealtime on The Office.
我们俩，还有整个演职人员团队，对《办公室》的用餐时间都有着非常特别的回忆。

1136
00:49:39.550 --> 00:49:45.330
Well, I just can't say enough about how these two teams kept our set going.
我怎么夸这两个团队都不为过，是他们支撑起了我们的片场。

1137
00:49:45.790 --> 00:49:47.490
You know, we were stuck.
你知道，我们当时被困在片场。

1138
00:49:47.770 --> 00:49:50.030
We can't go out for food or snacks.
我们没法出去买吃的或零食。

1139
00:49:50.030 --> 00:49:52.270
We're totally dependent on these teaMs.
我们完全依赖这些团队。

1140
00:49:52.270 --> 00:49:57.190
And I just, I was thinking back on all the ways that they would take care of us.
我刚才在回想他们照顾我们的点点滴滴。

1141
00:49:57.370 --> 00:50:01.990
Like, the little things, like if we were shooting someplace outside and we were cold,
比如一些小事，如果我们是在户外拍摄，感到冷的时候，

1142
00:50:02.810 --> 00:50:06.970
you know, Peter and Vartan would put out hot soup to warm us up, you know?
彼得和瓦尔坦就会准备热汤来帮我们暖身，你懂吗？

1143
00:50:07.270 --> 00:50:11.410
And all the care that Sergio took in our meals.
还有塞尔吉奥在准备餐点时所付出的所有心血。

1144
00:50:11.410 --> 00:50:15.170
Even making special meals when our kids came to set.
甚至在我们孩子来片场时，还会专门为他们做饭。

1145
00:50:16.060 --> 00:50:21.930
And, I mean, Jenna, I don't know how we would have gotten through our pregnancies without Peter and Vartan.
而且，珍娜，我不知道如果没有彼得和瓦尔坦，我们该怎么熬过孕期。

1146
00:50:22.350 --> 00:50:23.010
I know.
我知道。

1147
00:50:23.210 --> 00:50:26.090
They really fed us and nurtured us.
他们真的把我们喂得很好，也照顾得很好。

1148
00:50:26.270 --> 00:50:30.930
And, you know, I found a journal entry where I wrote about Peter and Vartan.
而且，我翻到了一篇日记，里面写到了彼得和瓦尔坦。

1149
00:50:31.150 --> 00:50:33.090
Oh, are you going to read it?
噢，你要读出来吗？

1150
00:50:33.190 --> 00:50:33.870
Yeah, I'm going to read it.
是的，我要读出来。

1151
00:50:33.870 --> 00:50:34.310
Okay, great.
好的，太棒了。

1152
00:50:34.310 --> 00:50:40.090
It's just, it's a real short little entry, but it just speaks to how they took care of us.
这只是……这只是一条很短的记录，但它恰好说明了他们是如何照顾我们的。

1153
00:50:40.590 --> 00:50:45.710
So, at the top, it says July 21st, 2011, 4.02 p.m.
在最上面写着：2011年7月21日下午4点02分。

1154
00:50:45.890 --> 00:50:48.030
You know, I always say what time it is.
你知道的，我总是会记下时间。

1155
00:50:48.590 --> 00:50:54.410
And I wrote, I had the day off from work today, but I had to go in for a wardrobe fitting.
我写道：今天我不用上班，但我得去参加服装试装。

1156
00:50:54.650 --> 00:50:56.270
I brought Isabel with me.
我带上了伊莎贝尔。

1157
00:50:56.710 --> 00:51:01.090
After my fitting, we had lunch on set, and Peter and Vartan were so sweet.
试装结束后，我们在片场吃了午饭，彼得和瓦尔坦人真的太好了。

1158
00:51:01.170 --> 00:51:05.650
They brought Isabel a special snack, cupcakes, and a smoothie.
他们给伊莎贝尔准备了特别的零食、纸杯蛋糕和冰沙。

1159
00:51:05.950 --> 00:51:06.470
Aw.
噢。

1160
00:51:06.730 --> 00:51:08.130
We had such a fun day.
我们度过了非常愉快的一天。

1161
00:51:08.130 --> 00:51:10.050
I love that, lady.
我喜欢这个，亲爱的。

1162
00:51:10.210 --> 00:51:11.510
Isn't that so cute?
这不是很可爱吗？

1163
00:51:12.230 --> 00:51:17.170
Well, lady, I don't think there is anyone on our set who loved our food more than BJ Novak.
嗯，亲爱的，我觉得在我们片场，没有谁比BJ·诺瓦克更爱我们的食物了。

1164
00:51:17.610 --> 00:51:20.010
BJ is like a foodie.
BJ是个美食家。

1165
00:51:20.150 --> 00:51:21.670
Like, for real, he's a foodie.
真的，他是那种真正的美食家。

1166
00:51:21.730 --> 00:51:23.950
He has a whole business now called Eat-A-Chain.
他现在有个完整的生意，叫“Eat-A-Chain”。

1167
00:51:24.050 --> 00:51:24.950
I know, right?
可不是吗？

1168
00:51:24.950 --> 00:51:33.290
And it's like Michelin star chefs turn your fast food favorites into, like, these elevated meals.
就像是米其林星级厨师把你最爱的快餐变成那种高级料理一样。

1169
00:51:33.510 --> 00:51:33.790
Right.
没错。

1170
00:51:34.030 --> 00:51:34.790
And they're delicious.
而且非常美味。

1171
00:51:34.830 --> 00:51:36.470
I went to the Chili's one.
我去过那个 Chili's 的主题活动。

1172
00:51:36.750 --> 00:51:38.250
I've been to two now.
我现在已经去过两次了。

1173
00:51:38.490 --> 00:51:39.670
One I took the kids with.
有一次我带了孩子们一起去。

1174
00:51:39.810 --> 00:51:42.290
They had a pop-up of all these different types of food chains.
他们搞了一个快闪店，汇集了各种不同类型的连锁餐饮。

1175
00:51:42.790 --> 00:51:43.310
Delicious.
太美味了。

1176
00:51:43.850 --> 00:51:44.570
So good.
太棒了。

1177
00:51:44.690 --> 00:51:45.130
So good.
太棒了。

1178
00:51:45.350 --> 00:51:51.010
Well, he invited our catering craft service teams to be on the DVD commentary track for season five,
他曾邀请我们的餐饮和后勤服务团队参加第五季的DVD评论音轨录制，

1179
00:51:51.170 --> 00:51:52.170
Business Ethics.
就是《商业道德》那一集。

1180
00:51:52.570 --> 00:51:53.210
I remember.
我记得。

1181
00:51:53.210 --> 00:51:54.810
So I reached out to him.
所以我联系了他。

1182
00:51:55.030 --> 00:51:57.810
And lady, I don't know if he's ever responded to me faster.
亲爱的，我不知道他有没有哪次回复我比这次更快的。

1183
00:51:58.250 --> 00:52:00.290
He is so excited about food.
他对食物真是太兴奋了。

1184
00:52:00.310 --> 00:52:04.190
I remember when I came across that commentary years ago and I texted him.
我记得多年前我偶然发现那段评论时，还给他发了短信。

1185
00:52:04.330 --> 00:52:05.330
He was like, no way.
他当时说：不会吧。

1186
00:52:05.330 --> 00:52:06.570
Where can I find it?
我在哪能找到它？

1187
00:52:06.770 --> 00:52:09.230
He was so excited that it still lives somewhere.
他非常激动，没想到那段内容居然还留存在某个地方。

1188
00:52:09.510 --> 00:52:09.690
Yeah.
是啊。

1189
00:52:09.950 --> 00:52:12.030
Well, he sent in an audio clip.
他发来了一段音频。

1190
00:52:12.370 --> 00:52:16.270
He has some advice for people who might be new to a set.
他给那些刚进片场的新人提了一些建议。

1191
00:52:16.730 --> 00:52:18.250
Oh, I can't wait to hear this.
噢，我迫不及待想听听了。

1192
00:52:18.250 --> 00:52:19.390
How to get the best stuff.
关于如何搞到最好的东西。

1193
00:52:20.310 --> 00:52:32.910
If I have any advice in show business, I have one piece of advice that I'm 100% sure of that I tell everyone, which is that if you want coffee on a set, get it from craft services,
如果我在演艺圈有什么建议的话，我有一条百分之百确定的建议要告诉所有人，那就是如果你想在片场喝咖啡，一定要去后勤服务台拿，

1194
00:52:32.910 --> 00:52:35.230
not catering.
不要去餐饮车拿。

1195
00:52:35.230 --> 00:52:40.870
When you arrive in the morning, there's going to be a truck that has all types of great food and they're going to have coffee on that truck.
当你早上到达时，会有一辆卡车提供各种很棒的食物，那辆车上也会有咖啡。

1196
00:52:41.030 --> 00:52:45.510
Do not get the coffee from the truck because they make coffee as an afterthought.
千万别喝那辆车上的咖啡，因为他们做咖啡只是顺带的。

1197
00:52:45.510 --> 00:52:48.810
Then there's craft services, which makes snacks and all that stuff.
然后是后勤服务台，他们负责提供零食之类的东西。

1198
00:52:48.910 --> 00:52:50.650
But coffee is what they do.
但咖啡才是他们的主业。

1199
00:52:50.890 --> 00:52:52.190
That's what they're judged on.
那是衡量他们工作好坏的标准。

1200
00:52:52.670 --> 00:52:54.430
Go the extra 20 feet.
多走那20英尺吧。

1201
00:52:54.590 --> 00:52:59.050
Get your coffee from craft services, not catering.
去茶水间拿咖啡，别去餐饮部拿。

1202
00:52:59.710 --> 00:53:03.250
Catering is great, but coffee is not their thing.
餐饮部很棒，但咖啡不是他们的强项。

1203
00:53:03.450 --> 00:53:05.310
It's not their focus, nor should it be.
那不是他们的重点，也不该是。

1204
00:53:08.430 --> 00:53:10.070
Hashes in his voice.
他说话带点沙哑。

1205
00:53:10.310 --> 00:53:17.730
Like he is literally telling people where to get coffee on a set the way I beg people to go get their cancer screenings.
他就像在片场叮嘱大家去哪儿喝咖啡一样，就像我求大家去做癌症筛查那样。

1206
00:53:17.730 --> 00:53:19.330
It cracked me up.
这把我逗乐了。

1207
00:53:19.470 --> 00:53:23.210
The absolute like seriousness.
那种绝对的严肃感。

1208
00:53:23.630 --> 00:53:23.910
Yes.
没错。

1209
00:53:24.350 --> 00:53:26.330
And he's right.
而且他是对的。

1210
00:53:26.570 --> 00:53:27.390
He is right.
他是对的。

1211
00:53:27.550 --> 00:53:37.470
I don't drink coffee, as you know, but I know craft services, they are sort of connoisseurs of like beverages and they do smoothies.
如你所知，我不喝咖啡，但我知道茶水间的人，他们算是饮料方面的行家，还会做冰沙。

1212
00:53:37.630 --> 00:53:38.430
They do coffee.
他们负责咖啡。

1213
00:53:38.570 --> 00:53:39.670
They do hot cocoa.
他们负责热可可。

1214
00:53:40.210 --> 00:53:43.410
I mean, they have a gazillion types of teas.
我是说，他们有成千上万种茶。

1215
00:53:43.790 --> 00:53:45.770
Like they are where you go for beverage.
他们就是你找饮料该去的地方。

1216
00:53:46.010 --> 00:53:46.510
Correct.
没错。

1217
00:53:47.170 --> 00:53:54.470
He also talked a little bit about the food in the writer's room, which is not provided by craft services or catering.
他还谈到了一点编剧室的食物，那不是由茶水间或餐饮部提供的。

1218
00:53:54.590 --> 00:53:55.230
That's right.
确实如此。

1219
00:53:55.430 --> 00:53:59.350
They have their own writer's assistant who has to manage food for the writers.
他们有自己的编剧助理，负责管理编剧们的伙食。

1220
00:53:59.370 --> 00:54:05.010
And, you know, this is because their hours would sometimes, they didn't coordinate with our hours.
你知道，这是因为他们的工作时间有时和我们的对不上。

1221
00:54:05.250 --> 00:54:07.850
Like they would be there writing until like 10 p.m.
他们有时会写到晚上10点。

1222
00:54:07.870 --> 00:54:08.250
or midnight.
或者午夜。

1223
00:54:08.570 --> 00:54:10.450
And then they also don't come in till 10 a.m.
而且他们有时要到上午10点才来。

1224
00:54:10.590 --> 00:54:10.950
sometimes.
有时是这样。

1225
00:54:11.250 --> 00:54:11.550
Yes.
是的。

1226
00:54:11.550 --> 00:54:15.610
So they kind of had their whole own food situation.
所以他们有自己的一套饮食安排。

1227
00:54:15.730 --> 00:54:17.950
And here's what he had to say about that.
以下是他对此的看法。

1228
00:54:18.370 --> 00:54:21.670
Snacks are it's like when you're a babysitter.
零食就像你当保姆的时候一样。

1229
00:54:21.670 --> 00:54:26.930
It's all about what the people's cabinets have, what snacks they have.
全看雇主橱柜里有什么，有什么零食。

1230
00:54:27.570 --> 00:54:28.990
And same for a writer's room.
编剧室也一样。

1231
00:54:29.110 --> 00:54:30.090
It's what snacks are there.
全看那儿有什么零食。

1232
00:54:30.170 --> 00:54:32.230
And we went through periods where we had every snack in the world.
我们经历过拥有世上所有零食的时期。

1233
00:54:32.450 --> 00:54:36.230
It was turkey jerky from Trader Joe's was the favorite snack.
Trader Joe's的火鸡肉干是最受欢迎的零食。

1234
00:54:36.230 --> 00:54:40.430
But it was all of these terribly salty Trader Joe's snacks.
但全是那些咸得要命的Trader Joe's零食。

1235
00:54:40.830 --> 00:54:43.570
And then every now and then we get disgusted with ourselves.
然后每隔一段时间，我们就会对自己感到厌恶。

1236
00:54:43.790 --> 00:54:51.110
We'd gain a lot of weight and we would ban all unhealthy foods from the writer's room and put them in the fridge and freezer by set.
我们会胖很多，然后禁止所有不健康的食物进入编剧室，把它们放进片场的冰箱和冷冻柜里。

1237
00:54:51.250 --> 00:54:56.530
So you could get an ice cream cone, but you had to walk to the freezer in the other trailer.
所以你想吃冰淇淋甜筒的话，就得走到另一辆拖车的冷冻柜那儿去。

1238
00:54:56.530 --> 00:54:58.270
And then we would slip.
然后我们又会破戒。

1239
00:54:58.450 --> 00:54:59.210
It would just be a cycle.
这简直是个循环。

1240
00:55:00.030 --> 00:55:07.650
So this is exactly how I remember the writer's room snacks, too, because I remember they had this back stairwell that went up to their kitchen.
我对编剧室零食的记忆也是这样，因为我记得他们有个通往厨房的后楼梯。

1241
00:55:07.810 --> 00:55:14.110
And sometimes we went up that way and it would be either feast or famine in there.
有时我们从那儿上去，里面要么是盛宴，要么是饥荒。

1242
00:55:14.210 --> 00:55:23.650
It would either be like seriously every type of like little Debbie cupcake or whatever to then just like nothing.
要么是各种各样的Little Debbie纸杯蛋糕之类的，要么就什么都没有。

1243
00:55:23.650 --> 00:55:26.370
Nothing are just like a rice cake.
什么都没有，或者只有米饼。

1244
00:55:26.730 --> 00:55:30.130
Yes, they did go through a whole like rice cake phase.
没错，他们确实经历过一阵子米饼热潮。

1245
00:55:30.430 --> 00:55:30.590
Yeah.
是啊。

1246
00:55:30.850 --> 00:55:35.870
And then when they were going through that phase, that's when they got like a treadmill, remember?
然后当他们经历那个阶段时，他们还弄了台跑步机，记得吗？

1247
00:55:36.730 --> 00:55:40.490
But yeah, there was a real yo-yo effect with their snacks.
没错，他们的零食确实有种溜溜球效应。

1248
00:55:41.030 --> 00:55:45.730
Well, you know, our first AD, Kelly Cantley, I was texting with her and I said,
嗯，你知道，我们的第一副导演Kelly Cantley，我当时在给她发短信，我说，

1249
00:55:45.850 --> 00:55:49.870
Hey, we're going to talk to Sergio for this food episode.
嘿，我们要和Sergio聊聊这期食物主题的节目。

1250
00:55:50.190 --> 00:55:52.850
I'm curious, like, what's your breakfast order?
我很好奇，你的早餐通常点什么？

1251
00:55:52.850 --> 00:55:59.910
Well, lady, she gave me the scoop on her breakfast order and also Sergio's doing something new.
好吧，女士，她跟我透露了她的早餐点餐习惯，而且Sergio最近在搞些新花样。

1252
00:56:00.170 --> 00:56:10.890
She said that on the office, her breakfast order was either a baby burrito with bacon and no salsa or one scrambled egg with a side of black beans and avocado.
她说在《办公室》剧组时，她的早餐要么是一个培根小卷饼，不要莎莎酱，要么是一个炒蛋配黑豆和牛油果。

1253
00:56:11.410 --> 00:56:14.430
Black beans and avocado, it's big on our set.
黑豆配牛油果，在我们片场很流行。

1254
00:56:14.430 --> 00:56:25.630
But she said on the paper, Sergio has updated all the things that she likes and now serves breakfast as a mini taco.
但她说在《办公室》的时候，Sergio更新了所有她喜欢的餐点，现在早餐做成了迷你塔可。

1255
00:56:26.370 --> 00:56:27.510
I mean.
我是说。

1256
00:56:27.890 --> 00:56:28.290
Yeah.
没错。

1257
00:56:28.470 --> 00:56:38.150
He takes one tater tot and he smashes it in the bottom of each mini taco and then he'll put whatever your breakfast order is inside.
他拿一个炸薯球，把它压扁铺在每个迷你塔可的底部，然后把你的早餐配料放进去。

1258
00:56:38.150 --> 00:56:40.030
She said, it's genius.
她说，这简直是天才之举。

1259
00:56:40.350 --> 00:56:41.370
Sign me up.
算我一个。

1260
00:56:41.490 --> 00:56:43.190
You had me at smash tater tot.
听到“压扁炸薯球”我就被征服了。

1261
00:56:43.490 --> 00:56:47.690
She said if he had a taco stand or a restaurant, I would go every day.
她说如果他开了塔可摊或者餐厅，她每天都会去光顾。

1262
00:56:48.190 --> 00:56:49.390
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1263
00:56:49.610 --> 00:56:50.870
That sounds so good.
听起来太棒了。

1264
00:56:51.290 --> 00:56:55.470
Well, you know, I was trading texts with Sergio about being on the podcaSt.
嗯，你知道，我之前和Sergio互发短信，聊到让他上播客的事。

1265
00:56:55.950 --> 00:57:00.850
Talk about someone who responded right away with such enthusiasm, much like BJ.
说起回复速度，他跟BJ一样，特别积极热情。

1266
00:57:00.850 --> 00:57:03.790
He could not wait to talk to us.
他迫不及待地想和我们聊天。

1267
00:57:03.930 --> 00:57:09.110
He's such a lovely person and we had so much fun going down memory lane with him.
他是个非常可爱的人，我们和他一起回忆往事，玩得很开心。

1268
00:57:09.270 --> 00:57:09.670
We did.
确实如此。

1269
00:57:09.910 --> 00:57:13.950
We Zoomed with him the other day and we can't wait for you to hear our chat with him.
我们前几天和他进行了视频通话，迫不及待想让你们听听我们的谈话。

1270
00:57:14.070 --> 00:57:16.070
So here is our chat with Sergio.
那么，这就是我们与Sergio的对话。

1271
00:57:19.270 --> 00:57:20.490
Hello, Sergio.
你好，Sergio。

1272
00:57:21.030 --> 00:57:21.570
Hi there.
你好。

1273
00:57:21.810 --> 00:57:21.910
Hi, Louise.
你好，Louise。

1274
00:57:22.510 --> 00:57:23.030
Thanks.
谢谢。

1275
00:57:23.590 --> 00:57:25.330
Thank you for coming on the podcaSt.
谢谢你来参加我们的播客。

1276
00:57:25.850 --> 00:57:28.050
I love the podcast, by the way.
顺便说一下，我很喜欢这个播客。

1277
00:57:28.310 --> 00:57:31.210
You all have nice voices, so it's soothing to the ear.
你们的声音都很好听，听起来很悦耳。

1278
00:57:31.210 --> 00:57:34.170
Yeah, it's funny and it's a lot of fun.
是啊，这节目很有趣，也很好玩。

1279
00:57:34.710 --> 00:57:35.750
Aw, thanks, Sergio.
噢，谢谢你，Sergio。

1280
00:57:36.170 --> 00:57:39.770
It was so nice seeing you when we visited the paper.
我们去《办公室》片场探班时见到你真是太好了。

1281
00:57:40.170 --> 00:57:40.650
I know.
我知道。

1282
00:57:40.830 --> 00:57:41.350
I like that.
我喜欢那样。

1283
00:57:41.530 --> 00:57:42.910
That was such a surprise.
那真是一个惊喜。

1284
00:57:43.290 --> 00:57:47.790
We were slammed for breakfast, but it was nice seeing you guys.
当时我们早餐时间忙得不可开交，但能见到你们真好。

1285
00:57:47.970 --> 00:57:56.090
And also being on that show, you know, kind of like, you know, having some of the crew members from the office and, you know, Oscar.
还有能上那个节目，你知道，就像是和《办公室》的一些剧组成员，还有Oscar一起。

1286
00:57:56.550 --> 00:57:58.450
It was awesome doing that show, too.
能做那个节目也很棒。

1287
00:57:58.530 --> 00:58:00.730
It just brings a lot of memories.
它勾起了很多回忆。

1288
00:58:01.210 --> 00:58:03.130
Of what we had in the office, you know?
关于我们在《办公室》时的点滴，你懂的？

1289
00:58:03.390 --> 00:58:05.290
Well, Sergio, you are so loved.
嗯，Sergio，大家都很爱你。

1290
00:58:05.530 --> 00:58:11.050
I have noticed pretty much every time I'm on a set where Mindy's running the show, you're there.
我注意到几乎每次我在Mindy负责的剧组时，你都在那儿。

1291
00:58:11.230 --> 00:58:15.450
Like, the office family loves you and they always want to work with you.
就像《办公室》大家庭都很爱你，总是想和你一起工作。

1292
00:58:15.770 --> 00:58:17.490
Yeah, no, I appreciate that.
是啊，不，我很感激。

1293
00:58:17.710 --> 00:58:23.630
It's been amazing being part of the office, you know, because we had a lot of great times, right?
能成为《办公室》的一员真是太棒了，你知道，因为我们有过很多美好的时光，对吧？

1294
00:58:23.630 --> 00:58:25.950
It was such an amazing time.
那真是一段美妙的时光。

1295
00:58:26.170 --> 00:58:31.050
And for me as a cook and cooking for y'all, it was special.
对我这个厨师来说，能为你们做饭，感觉很特别。

1296
00:58:31.510 --> 00:58:40.150
You know, you mentioned breakfast and Kelly shared with us that you have started doing mini tacos for breakfaSt.
你知道，你提到了早餐，Kelly跟我们分享说你开始做迷你塔可当早餐了。

1297
00:58:40.430 --> 00:58:47.330
She said you took her breakfast order and put it in a tiny taco and she said she can't get enough of it.
她说你把她的早餐点餐做成了迷你塔可，她说她怎么吃都吃不够。

1298
00:58:47.330 --> 00:58:49.710
Yeah, Kelly, it was awesome working with Kelly.
是啊，Kelly，和Kelly一起工作太棒了。

1299
00:58:50.030 --> 00:58:53.750
And yeah, she has like little orders, small orders, kind of like Angela.
而且，她点的餐都很小份，有点像Angela。

1300
00:58:54.190 --> 00:58:56.850
When Angela used to order her little Angela size.
以前Angela总是点她那种“Angela分量”的小份餐。

1301
00:58:57.230 --> 00:58:58.150
Yeah, Angie size.
没错，安吉的尺寸。

1302
00:58:58.570 --> 00:59:00.810
Yeah, that was fun.
是啊，那很有趣。

1303
00:59:01.250 --> 00:59:05.230
So, Sergio, you have been in this food business for so long.
那么，塞尔吉奥，你从事餐饮业已经这么久了。

1304
00:59:05.390 --> 00:59:08.330
How do you keep coming up with new ideas and new recipes?
你是如何不断想出新点子和新食谱的呢？

1305
00:59:08.330 --> 00:59:11.910
We're so curious how you put a menu together for the week.
我们很好奇你是如何安排每周菜单的。

1306
00:59:12.330 --> 00:59:18.270
Well, when I started the office, it was hard because there was no iPhone, right?
嗯，我刚开始做这一行时很困难，因为那时候还没有iPhone，对吧？

1307
00:59:18.450 --> 00:59:22.590
And I had to go through the cookbooks, you know, and just get the ideas from there.
我得翻阅各种食谱，你知道的，从里面找灵感。

1308
00:59:22.730 --> 00:59:26.290
And the feedback from the crew, that's kind of what you work with.
还有来自剧组的反馈，这基本上就是你工作的依据。

1309
00:59:26.430 --> 00:59:27.510
Like, oh, they like this.
比如，哦，他们喜欢这个。

1310
00:59:27.510 --> 00:59:30.090
So, you know, we're going that direction.
所以，你知道，我们就往那个方向做。

1311
00:59:30.290 --> 00:59:33.830
But yeah, it got easier when the iPhone came around, you know.
但确实，有了iPhone之后就容易多了，你知道的。

1312
00:59:34.010 --> 00:59:36.310
So it was just a lot easier.
所以真的轻松了很多。

1313
00:59:36.550 --> 00:59:40.670
But yeah, it was through crew members, what they like and all that.
不过，确实主要是通过剧组成员，看他们喜欢什么之类的。

1314
00:59:40.670 --> 00:59:46.730
So I have to ask you, you know, you're using word of mouth about what's a hit, what's not.
所以我得问问你，你是通过口碑来判断什么受欢迎，什么不受欢迎吗？

1315
00:59:47.250 --> 00:59:51.730
Was there a recipe you ever did that people were like, don't do that one again?
有没有哪道菜是你做过之后，大家说“别再做那道了”的？

1316
00:59:52.110 --> 00:59:55.130
Or was there one where everyone was like, you have to do that one again?
或者有没有哪道菜是大家说“你一定要再做一次”的？

1317
00:59:55.290 --> 00:59:58.030
Like, what are your hits and your misses?
也就是说，你有哪些成功之作和失败之作？

1318
00:59:58.510 --> 01:00:01.570
They never really tell you like, oh, that wasn't good.
他们其实从来不会直接说“哦，那道菜不好吃”。

1319
01:00:01.770 --> 01:00:05.030
You know, I only got that once.
你知道，我只遇到过一次这种情况。

1320
01:00:05.190 --> 01:00:08.350
And that was the Teamsters in New York, you know, one time.
那是纽约的卡车司机工会，你知道的，就那一次。

1321
01:00:08.350 --> 01:00:11.730
But only like as a family, like they already liked me a lot.
但那就像家人一样，因为他们本来就很喜欢我。

1322
01:00:12.010 --> 01:00:13.430
And they told me, hey, we love you.
他们对我说，嘿，我们很喜欢你。

1323
01:00:13.590 --> 01:00:18.270
But that last meal, you know, that's the only time they told me.
但那顿饭，你知道，那是他们唯一一次那样说。

1324
01:00:18.510 --> 01:00:20.410
But it was the Teamsters in New York, you know.
不过那是纽约的卡车司机工会，你知道的。

1325
01:00:20.590 --> 01:00:25.210
But other than that, with the office and all that, everybody was so nice.
除此之外，在办公室和其他地方，每个人都非常友善。

1326
01:00:25.410 --> 01:00:25.990
It was beautiful.
那感觉真好。

1327
01:00:26.590 --> 01:00:28.150
Well, your food is amazing.
嗯，你的厨艺太棒了。

1328
01:00:28.430 --> 01:00:31.230
That's why I couldn't believe anyone would ever tell you this was a miss.
所以我真不敢相信会有人跟你说那是失败之作。

1329
01:00:31.430 --> 01:00:35.490
But, you know, Jenna and I both had so many meals that we loved.
不过，你知道，珍娜和我都有很多非常喜欢的餐点。

1330
01:00:35.490 --> 01:00:37.550
What was your most requested meal?
你被点餐次数最多的是哪道菜？

1331
01:00:38.270 --> 01:00:40.150
The most requested meal?
被点餐次数最多？

1332
01:00:40.430 --> 01:00:46.690
It's the action stations, you know, like the pasta bars, the taco bars.
是现场制作台，你知道的，比如意面吧、塔可吧。

1333
01:00:46.750 --> 01:00:50.310
The crew always loved that, the action stations.
剧组总是很喜欢那个，现场制作台。

1334
01:00:50.670 --> 01:00:59.150
So every time we had like a fun station and, you know, especially the pasta bar and the taco bar, those are always a hit.
所以每次我们有那种有趣的餐台，你知道，尤其是意面吧和塔可吧，总是大受欢迎。

1335
01:00:59.150 --> 01:01:01.690
Well, I remember your pasta bar.
嗯，我记得你的意面吧。

1336
01:01:01.910 --> 01:01:02.750
I was a fan.
我是它的粉丝。

1337
01:01:03.210 --> 01:01:08.690
And you would have like all the different pastas and all the different ingredients and then different sauces.
你会准备各种不同的意面、各种配料，还有不同的酱汁。

1338
01:01:08.970 --> 01:01:11.510
And it was kind of like an omelet bar.
那感觉就像煎蛋卷吧一样。

1339
01:01:11.670 --> 01:01:16.370
You just walk up and point to all the things you wanted and you guys would make it right there on the spot.
你走过去指着你想要的所有东西，你们就会当场做好。

1340
01:01:16.590 --> 01:01:17.030
Yeah.
没错。

1341
01:01:17.210 --> 01:01:18.190
It was so great.
那真是太棒了。

1342
01:01:18.470 --> 01:01:19.250
It was fun.
很有趣。

1343
01:01:19.470 --> 01:01:20.630
I tried and have it.
我试着去吃过。

1344
01:01:20.630 --> 01:01:27.050
So when like also when Isabella, when she was young, she used to just eat plain pasta, right?
还有，当伊莎贝拉还小的时候，她总是只吃清淡的意面，对吧？

1345
01:01:27.350 --> 01:01:27.690
Yeah.
是的。

1346
01:01:28.010 --> 01:01:29.370
That was her go-to.
那是她的首选。

1347
01:01:29.670 --> 01:01:35.230
So, you know, it reminds me of that too, when Isabella was young coming to set.
所以，你知道，这让我想起了伊莎贝拉小时候来片场的情景。

1348
01:01:35.630 --> 01:01:37.310
You were so sweet with her.
你对她真是太贴心了。

1349
01:01:37.550 --> 01:01:41.350
You would always set aside a little buttered noodles dish for her.
你总是会特意为她留一份黄油拌面。

1350
01:01:41.710 --> 01:01:44.710
You took such good care of all of us in that way.
你一直以来都那样无微不至地照顾我们所有人。

1351
01:01:44.730 --> 01:01:45.070
Yeah.
是啊。

1352
01:01:45.070 --> 01:01:50.210
You know, we grew into a family there and there's nothing like that, you know, ever going to happen again.
你知道，我们在那儿处成了一家人，那种感觉，你知道，再也不会有了。

1353
01:01:50.350 --> 01:01:52.130
I don't think once in a lifetime.
我觉得这辈子也就这一次了。

1354
01:01:52.910 --> 01:02:02.970
Another thing, Sergio, is that you were able to like make a meal that was good for the people who were dairy-free and gluten-free and vegetarian.
还有一件事，塞尔吉奥，你总能做出既适合不吃乳制品的人，又适合不吃麸质的人，还适合素食者吃的美味餐点。

1355
01:02:03.030 --> 01:02:07.190
And you would have a meat option, but then you would have also a fish option.
你既有肉类选择，也有鱼类选择。

1356
01:02:07.430 --> 01:02:08.550
How do you do it?
你是怎么做到的？

1357
01:02:08.630 --> 01:02:14.110
And also at breakfast, I never heard anybody order breakfast and you didn't have whatever the thing was.
而且早餐也是，我从来没听过有人点的早餐是你没准备好的。

1358
01:02:14.110 --> 01:02:20.330
Like, this is a silly question, but where do you keep all this food and who does the grocery shopping?
这问题听起来有点傻，但你把这些食物都存哪儿了？谁负责去买菜？

1359
01:02:20.510 --> 01:02:21.470
How do you do this?
你是怎么搞定这一切的？

1360
01:02:21.910 --> 01:02:22.150
Yeah.
是啊。

1361
01:02:22.390 --> 01:02:33.810
So, so when, when it started, you know, season one, um, the mise en place for breakfast was a little bit small, but as the show grew in the, into the years, you know,
所以，当第一季刚开始的时候，嗯，早餐的备料台还有点小，但随着节目一年年做下去，你知道，

1362
01:02:34.270 --> 01:02:38.130
like by the third season, you know, same crew members, the caSt.
到了第三季，你知道，还是那帮剧组成员和演员。

1363
01:02:38.130 --> 01:02:42.510
And, and so everybody had their little, you know, little specialty.
每个人都有自己的一点，你知道，一点小偏好。

1364
01:02:42.810 --> 01:02:52.530
So I had to make sure I had this, I had to make sure I had goat cheese because a couple of orders, you know, and it grew the mise en place for breakfaSt.
所以我得确保我有这个，我得确保我有山羊奶酪，因为有几个人点过，你知道，早餐的备料台就这么扩大了。

1365
01:02:52.850 --> 01:03:00.070
It grew like more and more as the years went on, but by the ninth season, I had a lot of stuff in the fridge.
随着年头增加，它越来越大，到第九季的时候，冰箱里已经塞满了东西。

1366
01:03:00.070 --> 01:03:02.790
But I bet, I bet you did.
我敢说，我敢说你肯定做了不少。

1367
01:03:03.050 --> 01:03:09.670
I mean, I feel like there were people who were like, I want my breakfast order, but will you throw some like hot peppers on it today?
我是说，我觉得有些人会说，我想吃我点的早餐，但你今天能往里面加点辣椒吗？

1368
01:03:09.870 --> 01:03:10.810
And you'd say, sure.
然后你就会说，没问题。

1369
01:03:11.230 --> 01:03:11.430
Yeah.
是啊。

1370
01:03:11.970 --> 01:03:12.530
No, yeah.
没错，是啊。

1371
01:03:12.810 --> 01:03:15.490
Especially I had, I had the Rashida special.
特别是，我还有那个“拉什达特供”。

1372
01:03:15.690 --> 01:03:16.910
That one was a hit, right?
那个很受欢迎，对吧？

1373
01:03:17.050 --> 01:03:18.210
Remember the Rashida special?
还记得“拉什达特供”吗？

1374
01:03:18.830 --> 01:03:20.530
That one was such a hit.
那个真的太受欢迎了。

1375
01:03:20.530 --> 01:03:22.090
So I had to have black beans.
所以我必须准备黑豆。

1376
01:03:22.330 --> 01:03:29.830
I had to have, you know, turkey bacon every day, every day, you know, that because corn tortillas, the green salsa, you know.
我必须准备，你知道，火鸡培根，每天都要，每天，你知道，还有玉米饼、绿莎莎酱，你知道的。

1377
01:03:30.330 --> 01:03:31.790
Yeah, that one really took off.
是啊，那个真的火了。

1378
01:03:32.030 --> 01:03:33.010
Yeah, it took off.
是啊，火起来了。

1379
01:03:33.130 --> 01:03:35.970
That took off for a while too.
那个也火了一阵子。

1380
01:03:36.470 --> 01:03:38.790
But, you know, Sergio, I was so curious.
但是，你知道，塞尔吉奥，我一直很好奇。

1381
01:03:38.790 --> 01:03:40.510
I've always wanted to ask you this.
我一直想问你这个。

1382
01:03:40.590 --> 01:03:43.150
How did you start as a chef?
你是怎么开始当厨师的？

1383
01:03:43.350 --> 01:03:45.450
What was your journey to doing this?
你走上这条路的过程是怎样的？

1384
01:03:45.450 --> 01:03:51.930
So I started, you know, this catering company as a dishwasher at 18.
我是在18岁时从洗碗工开始接触这家餐饮公司的。

1385
01:03:52.510 --> 01:03:54.830
And then I moved up, moved up the ranks.
然后我一步步晋升。

1386
01:03:55.030 --> 01:03:57.970
And then they gave me a shot, the catering company I was at.
后来他们给了我一个机会，就是我待的那家餐饮公司。

1387
01:03:58.090 --> 01:04:01.730
They gave me a shot as a chef, kind of young, like at 24.
他们给了我一个当厨师的机会，那时我还挺年轻的，大概24岁。

1388
01:04:01.810 --> 01:04:04.190
And I was like chef in commercials.
我当时是拍广告的厨师。

1389
01:04:04.450 --> 01:04:05.890
That's all I was doing.
我做的就只有这些。

1390
01:04:05.910 --> 01:04:08.470
So I had like five day recipes.
所以我只需要准备五天的食谱。

1391
01:04:08.470 --> 01:04:10.290
That's all I needed for commercials.
拍广告只需要这些。

1392
01:04:10.890 --> 01:04:14.370
And so then I got the call to do the office.
后来我接到了电话去负责《办公室》剧组。

1393
01:04:14.370 --> 01:04:20.890
So the office was my first show and like full on five days a week, months, you know.
所以《办公室》是我参与的第一个节目，那种全职的、一周五天、持续好几个月的，你知道。

1394
01:04:21.050 --> 01:04:22.450
So I was real nervous.
所以我当时真的很紧张。

1395
01:04:22.770 --> 01:04:24.570
Like I was nervous on the first day.
第一天的时候我特别紧张。

1396
01:04:24.790 --> 01:04:29.150
And then the second day, the craft service, then it was another craft.
然后第二天，那个茶点服务员，那是另一个茶点服务员。

1397
01:04:29.250 --> 01:04:31.250
It wasn't it wasn't Peter and Rotten.
不是彼得和罗滕。

1398
01:04:31.470 --> 01:04:35.910
But that craft service told me on the second day, it said they were talking about you.
但那个茶点服务员第二天跟我说，他说大家都在谈论你。

1399
01:04:36.190 --> 01:04:40.390
And I was like real horrified that they were like something.
我当时真的吓坏了，以为他们说了什么。

1400
01:04:41.050 --> 01:04:43.190
Yeah, and it was good news, right?
是啊，而且是好消息，对吧？

1401
01:04:43.330 --> 01:04:45.070
He says they were talking good about your food.
他说他们对你的厨艺评价很高。

1402
01:04:45.390 --> 01:04:48.610
And that gave me the confidence to try hard and all that.
这让我有了信心去努力尝试之类的。

1403
01:04:48.870 --> 01:04:51.450
And it was such a nice crew that it was easy to do.
而且剧组氛围很好，做起来也很轻松。

1404
01:04:51.830 --> 01:04:55.710
But I learned a lot through the office, you know, through the casting crew.
但我通过办公室，你知道，通过选角团队学到了很多。

1405
01:04:55.850 --> 01:05:01.410
I learned a lot like, you know, like through the cooking and took it, took it with me to the other shows.
我学到了很多，比如通过烹饪，然后我把这些经验带到了其他节目中。

1406
01:05:01.410 --> 01:05:03.950
But yeah, the office was my school.
但确实，办公室就是我的学校。

1407
01:05:04.390 --> 01:05:08.130
How much did you coordinate with Michael and Vartan?
你和迈克尔还有瓦尔坦协调得怎么样？

1408
01:05:08.310 --> 01:05:12.510
Because they would bring out like a certain hot snack every day at 10 o'clock.
因为他们每天十点都会带出某种热乎的小吃。

1409
01:05:12.710 --> 01:05:14.250
And did you guys talk?
你们会沟通吗？

1410
01:05:14.430 --> 01:05:21.190
Like, were you sure to be like, OK, if they're doing a hot dog bar, I'm not going to do hot dogs at lunch?
比如，你会确认一下，比如，好吧，如果他们要做热狗吧，我就不在午餐做热狗了吗？

1411
01:05:21.790 --> 01:05:22.690
We did.
我们确实会。

1412
01:05:22.930 --> 01:05:23.430
We tried.
我们尝试过。

1413
01:05:23.570 --> 01:05:31.390
But for some reason, we still always ended up doing the same thing, you know, kind of, you know, like, oh, you're doing that?
但不知为何，我们最后总是会做一样的东西，你知道，就是那种，噢，你们在做那个？

1414
01:05:32.370 --> 01:05:33.470
So, but yeah.
所以，确实是这样。

1415
01:05:33.650 --> 01:05:34.230
Oh, that's so funny.
噢，那太搞笑了。

1416
01:05:34.450 --> 01:05:36.110
I don't have that memory at all.
我完全没有那种记忆。

1417
01:05:36.270 --> 01:05:41.290
I was like, somehow you guys never managed to double up in my mind.
我当时觉得，不知怎么的，你们在我印象中从来没撞过菜。

1418
01:05:41.450 --> 01:05:42.390
OK, that's good.
好的，那很好。

1419
01:05:42.550 --> 01:05:46.470
Because, yeah, Peter and Vartan, you know, like we come up with something.
因为，彼得和瓦尔坦，你知道，我们想出点什么。

1420
01:05:46.630 --> 01:05:48.090
I'm doing that today.
我今天就做那个。

1421
01:05:48.090 --> 01:05:52.790
But yeah, they were so much fun, those two guys, man.
但说真的，那两个家伙太有趣了，伙计。

1422
01:05:52.890 --> 01:05:53.870
I loved them.
我很喜欢他们。

1423
01:05:54.150 --> 01:05:55.250
And I miss them.
我很想念他们。

1424
01:05:55.870 --> 01:05:56.910
Yeah, same.
我也是。

1425
01:05:57.310 --> 01:06:05.910
You know, Sergio, I'm so curious, too, because you are planning meals all the time and huge meals, too.
你知道，塞尔吉奥，我也很好奇，因为你一直在规划餐食，而且还是大餐。

1426
01:06:06.290 --> 01:06:08.110
Do you plan any meals at home?
你在家会规划餐食吗？

1427
01:06:08.270 --> 01:06:10.750
Are you just like once you're home, you are done meal planning?
还是说一旦回到家，你就彻底不想规划餐食了？

1428
01:06:11.270 --> 01:06:12.070
No, I am.
不，我会的。

1429
01:06:12.230 --> 01:06:12.750
I do.
我会规划。

1430
01:06:12.950 --> 01:06:16.230
I actually cook for my boys on the weekend.
周末我其实会为我的孩子们做饭。

1431
01:06:16.230 --> 01:06:18.510
I see them on the weekend.
我周末会见到他们。

1432
01:06:18.830 --> 01:06:21.110
So we do every weekend.
所以我们每个周末都会一起。

1433
01:06:21.290 --> 01:06:24.790
We I do a dinner and we watch movies.
我会做顿晚餐，然后我们一起看电影。

1434
01:06:24.990 --> 01:06:27.530
And I like to cook here, too.
我也喜欢在这里做饭。

1435
01:06:27.790 --> 01:06:31.690
It's a lot funner and, you know, get to experience new stuff.
这更有趣，而且，你知道，可以尝试新东西。

1436
01:06:31.830 --> 01:06:32.990
I like cooking at home.
我喜欢在家里做饭。

1437
01:06:33.190 --> 01:06:34.430
It's that when I'm working.
只是在我工作的时候。

1438
01:06:34.430 --> 01:06:39.170
If I'm working, then, you know, only that Saturday is the only day I'll cook.
如果我在工作，那么，你知道，只有周六是我会做饭的日子。

1439
01:06:39.370 --> 01:06:40.430
Oh, that's fair.
噢，那很公平。

1440
01:06:40.430 --> 01:06:47.470
Well, you know, I love your food so much that when I worked on the office,
嗯，你知道，我太喜欢你的食物了，以至于我在《办公室》工作时，

1441
01:06:47.470 --> 01:06:53.610
I would go through the lunch line and I would pick something for lunch and then I would wait for everybody to eat.
我会去午餐排队，挑点午餐吃，然后等大家都吃完。

1442
01:06:53.610 --> 01:07:03.930
And then as you all would start to kind of pack up stuff, like lunch was over, I would go through and I would get one of your to go containers and I would pick something.
然后当你们开始收拾东西，午餐结束时，我会再去拿一个外带盒，挑点东西。

1443
01:07:04.130 --> 01:07:05.610
And that's what I would eat for dinner.
那就是我晚餐要吃的东西。

1444
01:07:06.070 --> 01:07:07.510
Yeah, that's nice.
是啊，那真不错。

1445
01:07:07.690 --> 01:07:12.830
So I would eat your food twice a day for all those years on the office.
所以在《办公室》的那几年里，我每天都吃两次你做的饭。

1446
01:07:13.330 --> 01:07:14.210
Thank you so much.
非常感谢。

1447
01:07:14.310 --> 01:07:15.670
I appreciate that, Jenna.
我很感激，珍娜。

1448
01:07:15.890 --> 01:07:16.230
Thank you.
谢谢你。

1449
01:07:16.230 --> 01:07:20.650
Yeah, there was many times we were taking food home.
是啊，我们有很多次都把食物带回家了。

1450
01:07:20.950 --> 01:07:21.310
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

1451
01:07:21.950 --> 01:07:27.150
Sergio, do you have a favorite food memory from the office or a behind the scenes memory?
塞尔吉奥，你在《办公室》剧组里有没有什么关于食物的难忘回忆，或者幕后的趣事？

1452
01:07:27.410 --> 01:07:30.310
It doesn't have to be food related just from your time on the show.
不一定非得是关于食物的，只要是你在剧组期间的经历就行。

1453
01:07:31.430 --> 01:07:34.370
Yeah, it's my most memorable one.
有，那是我最难忘的一件事。

1454
01:07:34.570 --> 01:07:42.930
It was kind of a sad one, but it was Steve Carell's last day and we went to the warehouse and we did that beautiful speech.
虽然有点伤感，但那是史蒂夫·卡瑞尔在剧组的最后一天，我们去了仓库，发表了那段感人的演讲。

1455
01:07:42.930 --> 01:07:50.570
And then we took the time to talk to every department, you know, and I'll never forget it.
然后我们花时间与每个部门的人交谈，你知道，我永远不会忘记那一刻。

1456
01:07:50.710 --> 01:07:53.650
It's like, you know, there wasn't a dry eye in the room.
当时，你知道，屋子里没有一个人不流泪的。

1457
01:07:53.830 --> 01:07:58.330
Everybody was, it was the most memorable one that I'll never forget.
每个人都……那是我最难忘的经历，我永远不会忘记。

1458
01:07:59.030 --> 01:07:59.230
Yeah.
是的。

1459
01:08:00.030 --> 01:08:03.270
Have you run into Steve since the office wrapped?
《办公室》完结后，你见过史蒂夫吗？

1460
01:08:03.550 --> 01:08:03.890
Yes.
见过。

1461
01:08:03.890 --> 01:08:17.430
Yeah, so when Vartan passed away, I found out, you know, about it through Debbie and me, Alan, and Debbie went and we were right there at the funeral.
是的，瓦尔坦去世的时候，我是从黛比那里得知的，我和艾伦、黛比一起去了葬礼现场。

1462
01:08:17.910 --> 01:08:22.850
And then it was, you know, us three and in walks Steve Carell.
当时我们三个在那儿，然后史蒂夫·卡瑞尔走了进来。

1463
01:08:23.110 --> 01:08:26.710
And it was like, it was us four right there.
就像是，我们四个人聚在了一起。

1464
01:08:26.850 --> 01:08:28.770
And that's, you know, that's a beautiful moment.
那是一个非常美好的时刻。

1465
01:08:29.490 --> 01:08:33.650
And we got to, you know, talk with Steve Carell about the office.
我们还有机会和史蒂夫·卡瑞尔聊了聊《办公室》。

1466
01:08:34.070 --> 01:08:36.430
And that was the last time I saw him.
那是我最后一次见到他。

1467
01:08:36.790 --> 01:08:41.910
I also saw him on Space Force, but the last time was Vartan, I believe.
我也在《太空部队》里见过他，但最后一次见面应该是在瓦尔坦的葬礼上。

1468
01:08:42.450 --> 01:08:43.050
Yeah.
是啊。

1469
01:08:43.270 --> 01:08:52.250
I know several people have always asked us about the different menus on the show and what our favorite meal was.
我知道很多人一直问我们关于剧组里不同的菜单，以及我们最喜欢的餐点是什么。

1470
01:08:52.250 --> 01:08:56.250
And, you know, Sergio, my favorite was anything with your salsa.
而且，塞尔吉奥，我最喜欢的就是任何配上你莎莎酱的食物。

1471
01:08:56.530 --> 01:08:58.490
We've, I've talked about that a lot.
我们，我经常提到这一点。

1472
01:08:58.870 --> 01:09:03.350
But, Sergio, do you actually have a favorite dish for yourself?
但是，塞尔吉奥，你自己有没有最喜欢的一道菜？

1473
01:09:03.590 --> 01:09:05.910
Like, what is your favorite go-to snack?
比如，你最喜欢的零食是什么？

1474
01:09:06.190 --> 01:09:08.590
For a snack, I like the Chico stick.
零食的话，我喜欢奇科棒（Chico stick）。

1475
01:09:09.050 --> 01:09:09.730
Oh, yeah?
哦，是吗？

1476
01:09:10.150 --> 01:09:10.630
Yeah.
是的。

1477
01:09:12.350 --> 01:09:13.650
That's the one I like.
我就喜欢那个。

1478
01:09:13.730 --> 01:09:14.810
I just can't resist it.
我简直无法抗拒。

1479
01:09:14.890 --> 01:09:19.670
When I see that, it's not everywhere, but when it's there, I grab one, you know.
当我看到它的时候——虽然不是到处都有——但只要有，我就会拿一个。

1480
01:09:19.670 --> 01:09:23.770
But for food, it's tacos, you know.
但说到正餐，那就是塔可了。

1481
01:09:24.090 --> 01:09:27.410
I gotta say tacos with salsa and all that stuff.
我得说，配上莎莎酱和各种配料的塔可。

1482
01:09:27.570 --> 01:09:28.390
I love tacos.
我超爱塔可。

1483
01:09:28.730 --> 01:09:30.890
I also remember your dessert bar.
我还记得你的甜点吧。

1484
01:09:31.090 --> 01:09:35.610
You talk about action stations, but one time you had like a make-your-own-sunday bar.
你提到过现场制作区，有一次你还弄了个自制圣代吧。

1485
01:09:36.130 --> 01:09:38.690
And it was like amazing.
那简直太棒了。

1486
01:09:39.110 --> 01:09:39.330
Yeah.
是啊。

1487
01:09:39.510 --> 01:09:41.590
And it was like one of the more summer months.
那好像是在某个夏天。

1488
01:09:41.730 --> 01:09:45.970
And I just remember how good that bowl of ice cream and I got to put all my toppings on it.
我至今还记得那碗冰淇淋有多好吃，我往上面加了所有的配料。

1489
01:09:46.210 --> 01:09:49.250
But was there a standout dessert that people loved?
那么，有没有哪款甜点是大家特别喜欢的？

1490
01:09:49.670 --> 01:09:50.810
The cookie cake.
曲奇蛋糕。

1491
01:09:51.170 --> 01:09:51.730
Yes.
没错。

1492
01:09:51.850 --> 01:09:52.770
The hot cookie cake.
热乎乎的曲奇蛋糕。

1493
01:09:53.050 --> 01:09:57.910
That one was a must every day, actually, with ice cream.
那个其实每天都是必点的，还要配上冰淇淋。

1494
01:09:58.610 --> 01:09:58.710
Yeah.
是啊。

1495
01:09:58.790 --> 01:10:02.890
So it was on, you know, it's on a hot Schaefer.
它是放在，你知道，放在热的谢弗（Schaefer）餐盘上的。

1496
01:10:03.070 --> 01:10:05.530
So it's hot, nice and soft.
所以它热乎乎的，口感又软又好。

1497
01:10:05.750 --> 01:10:06.250
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

1498
01:10:06.710 --> 01:10:07.010
Yeah.
是啊。

1499
01:10:07.190 --> 01:10:08.350
That one's still a hit.
那个到现在还是很受欢迎。

1500
01:10:08.590 --> 01:10:13.950
But that's the one that, for sure, because it wasn't there at the beginning.
那绝对是大家的最爱，因为刚开始的时候还没有这道甜点。

1501
01:10:13.950 --> 01:10:16.990
It got there around, I think, season five or something.
我想大概是在第五季左右吧。

1502
01:10:16.990 --> 01:10:21.450
So once it got there, it was, we couldn't take it out no more.
一旦到了那个阶段，我们就再也离不开它了。

1503
01:10:21.750 --> 01:10:29.390
It had like this crusty, like I always wanted an edge piece because it would get nice and crispy around the edge.
它上面有一层硬皮，我总是想要边缘的那一块，因为边缘烤得又香又脆。

1504
01:10:29.510 --> 01:10:31.830
And that was Steve's favorite dessert.
那是史蒂夫最喜欢的甜点。

1505
01:10:32.050 --> 01:10:39.230
Steve and I would often meet at the warm chocolate chip cookie dish at the end of lunch.
我和史蒂夫经常在午餐结束时，在那盘温热的巧克力豆曲奇旁碰面。

1506
01:10:39.230 --> 01:10:40.610
And we would kind of laugh.
我们还会相视一笑。

1507
01:10:40.750 --> 01:10:42.310
We'd be like, here we are again.
就像在说，我们又见面了。

1508
01:10:42.330 --> 01:10:45.870
So we meet again over a warm chocolate chip cookie dessert.
所以我们又在温热的巧克力豆曲奇甜点旁相遇了。

1509
01:10:46.850 --> 01:10:48.190
I loved it.
我太喜欢了。

1510
01:10:48.610 --> 01:10:49.110
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

1511
01:10:49.290 --> 01:10:52.330
And also right there in stage three, right?
而且就在三号摄影棚那里，对吧？

1512
01:10:54.350 --> 01:10:59.910
That was so special because all of the cast was, you know, Steve ate there.
那段时光特别珍贵，因为所有的演员都在那儿，你知道的，史蒂夫也在那儿吃饭。

1513
01:11:00.110 --> 01:11:01.230
Everybody ate there.
每个人都在那儿吃。

1514
01:11:01.410 --> 01:11:04.330
The crew and then decisions were made there.
剧组人员，还有各种决定也是在那儿做出的。

1515
01:11:04.710 --> 01:11:06.810
Birthday parties celebrated there.
生日派对也是在那儿庆祝的。

1516
